 not what\" paragraph in `AGENTS.md` (symlinked as `CLAUDE.md`) with \"Doc comments on public API; elsewhere only where names fall short\". Public symbols keep the doc comment rule; non-public methods, types, and properties get a comment only when names and parameter labels don't make the behavior clear. Docs only, no code changes. Identical wording is going into swift-steward.\n\nWhy: on 2026-10-23 the maintainer asked that non-public code be commented only where names aren't clear enough, while public symbols keep their doc comments.\n\n## Review\n\n`codex review --base main` failed with HTTP 400 because the configured model (`gpt-6.1-sol`) was rejected for the ChatGPT account; `gpt-5.5` and `gpt-5-codex` failed the same way. The review was done instead by a fresh Claude subagent (Opus), given only the diff and the neighbouring rule. It reported 6 findings. **4 fixed, 2 declined**, in a follow-up commit (the wording no longer has to match swift-steward verbatim; the coordinator copies the final text over).\n\n1. Medium: \"Any comment ... explains why, not what\" could be read to cover the required public doc-comment summary. Fixed: scoped to \"Beyond the required public summary, keep every comment ...\".\n2. Medium: a comment allowed because a name isn't clear enough has to say what, but the paragraph then forbids \"what\". Declined: the rule's meaning is that a comment explains why, not what; a name that fails to carry the behavior is better fixed by renaming.\n3. Medium: the bold lead-in reads as a blanket restriction although public symbols are an exception. Fixed: the heading is now \"Doc comments on public API; elsewhere only where names fall short\".\n4. Low: \"one\" is ambiguous and the list of declarations omits initializers, enum cases and similar. Fixed: now \"doc comment\" and \"non-public declarations (methods, types, properties, and the like)\".\n5. Low: \"Keep them few\" was dropped. Declined: \"to the point\" and the why-not-what rule already limit density, and \"only where names fall short\" covers declarations.\n6. Nit: \"Any comment is to the point\" is a statement rather than an imperative, and \"parameter labels\" applies only to methods. Fixed: imperative \"keep every comment to the point\"; \"for methods, parameter labels\".\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-22T22:51:36Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T23:25:15Z","closed_at":"2026-10-22T23:25:14Z","merged_at":"2026-10-22T23:25:13Z","merge_commit_sha":"ae23a70101c9f41cbe1d301ed0295b28789bdd8f","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"marosoaie:claude/docs-comment-guidance-de5fe6","ref":"claude/docs-comment-guidance-de5fe6","repo":{"id":1430326489,"node_id":"R_kgDOVUEM2Q","name":"git-diff-parser","full_name":"marosoaie/git-diff-parser","owner":{"login":"marosoaie","id":2098985,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTg5ODU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2098985?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/marosoaie","html_url":"https://github.com/marosoaie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marosoaie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marosoaie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marosoaie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marosoaie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marosoaie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marosoaie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marosoaie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marosoaie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marosoaie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"private":false,"fork":false,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"description":"Streaming, zero-dependency Swift parser for unified git 